// Pell, jackdaw, journeyman (character-bibles.md §1). The Journeyman's Hall (Hall_2), Act 2.
// Voice: long, breathless, lists; "which, technically, means"; never unkind; speaks plainly. Image: lists that shorten.
// Interlude A (bible 7.2): the Minder's Report. Pell has written it; Wren can read it; Pell decides. Having read it,
// two or more Warden answers in Halden and Pell keeps it; otherwise Pell sends it, and reads it aloud to her face.
// Sent: Wardens hunt her in every anchored town (Licence), and Oriel (6.8).

title: Hall_Pell_Minder
---
<<if has_flag("pell.report_decided")>>
    <<jump Hall_Pell_After>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("halden.hall.pell_minder")>>
    <<jump Hall_Pell_Report>>
<<endif>>
Pell: Five things. No, three. Three things, I've been practising. #line:0552f00
Pell: The Hall thinks you drowned. Tam thinks you'll sit the exam with him. I think neither. #line:022f249
-> You wrote it down. #line:0728e36
    Pell: All of it. It's accurate. That's the whole problem, isn't it. #line:080f705
    <<voice surveyor halden>>
-> Then don't send it. #line:0ba9ea1
    Pell: If I don't, someone less accurate will. Which, technically, is worse for you. #line:04a89c8
    <<voice warden halden>>
-> ... #line:0028172
    Pell: You do that. Isolde did that. I always talked into it. #line:0ccb647
    <<voice drift halden>>
Pell: I'm to walk with you. Minder, they call it. Which means I tell them where you went. #line:0495cc4
<<flag halden.hall.pell_minder 1>>
===

title: Hall_Pell_Report
---
Pell: It's written. The report. I've read it four times. It doesn't get kinder. It gets more accurate. #line:0a62a83
-> Let me read it. #line:07fe2d8
    <<jump Hall_Pell_Read>>
-> Then send it. #line:0bdca4f
    Pell: That's what Isolde would say. Isolde isn't here. Which, technically, is the problem. #line:029dbb9
    <<jump Hall_Pell_Send>>
-> ... #line:09a6a9d
    Pell: Silence. You know I can't write that down. There isn't a column for it. #line:076e54a
    <<jump Hall_Pell_Send>>
===

title: Hall_Pell_Read
---
Report: Journeyman Wren entered the Greyfold without a tether and returned unchanged. #line:0b11359
Report: She carries the torn pages of Isolde Marr. She is unlicensed. She has not surrendered them. #line:07b7dd5
Report: She has, in the minder's view, been kind to everyone she has met. This is not relevant. #line:0da6dc2
Pell: It's accurate. That's the whole problem. #line:0e78ab4
<<flag pell.report_read 1>>
<<if voice_in("halden", "warden") >= 2>>
    Pell: You'd have carried me out. Of anywhere. I know that now. #line:06a7ad1
    Pell: One list. One item. I'm not sending it. #line:062ddd9
    <<flag pell.report_kept 1>>
    <<flag pell.report_decided 1>>
<<else>>
    <<jump Hall_Pell_Send>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Hall_Pell_Send
---
Pell: I'm sending it. I'm telling you to your face, because that's the only fair part. #line:0ffb172
Pell: Captain Oriel will read it. She reads everything twice. #line:08bda0b
<<flag pell.report_sent 1>>
<<flag pell.report_decided 1>>
===

title: Hall_Pell_After
---
<<if has_flag("pell.report_sent")>>
    Pell: Three things. The Wardens have it. Oriel has it. I have a copy. I read it at night. #still #line:00f594d
<<else>>
    Pell: One thing. It's in my drawer. It's still accurate. It stays there. #still #line:0845f6e
<<endif>>
===
